february is american heart month  according to the cdc more than 600  000 people die each year due to heart  disease part of the red cross's mission  to raise awareness  includes teaching more people cpr bianca  holman has our story  let's go 1 000 2 1 000 31 000 cpr  keeps blood and oxygen flowing it  dramatically increases the survival in  those who suffer from cardiac arrest  since february is heart health month the  american red cross is encouraging  everyone to take a cpr class  in an emergency situation there are  three basic steps  first call 9-1-1 next chest compressions  to keep blood flowing  finally using an aed cpr classes teach  the in-depth  proper technique to save a life with the  pandemic going on and more and more  people at home  you know we have to remember that  emergencies don't stop so just because  we have a pandemic  doesn't mean that other emergencies like  heart attacks aren't  aren't also happening with coveted  concerns there are trainings for  hands-on cpr where you only use chest  compressions  and not the mouth-to-mouth component for  more information on cpr classes visit  redcross.org  bianca holman 8 news now
 

